# =====================================================================================
# Cross-platform hygiene for this repo.
#
# Without this, checking out on Windows and pushing to a Linux CI causes two problems
# I have already hit: the Maven wrapper loses its executable bit and CI fails at the
# first ./mvnw call, and every commit spams "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings
# for every text file touched.
# =====================================================================================

# Default: normalise text files to LF in the repo, let the OS decide the working copy.
# This stops PowerShell CRLF endings from creeping into the committed blob.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and the Maven wrapper: LF and executable, no exceptions - Linux CI
# reads these and needs the exec bit set even when they were committed from Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers: always CRLF so cmd.exe parses them correctly.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: mark explicitly so git never tries to "fix" line endings inside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.jar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Keep large binary review noise out of `git diff` output.
docs/screenshots/** linguist-generated=true
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
